## Introduction & Overview

### What is PyCharm?

PyCharm is a professional integrated development environment (IDE) for Python development created by JetBrains.

**Key Facts:**
- **Type**: Full-featured IDE (not just a text editor)
- **Developer**: JetBrains (also makes IntelliJ IDEA, WebStorm, Android Studio)
- **Versions**: Community (free) and Professional (paid)
- **Platforms**: Windows, macOS, Linux
- **License**: Community = Apache 2.0, Professional = Commercial

### Why Use PyCharm?

**Advantages:**
- ✅ Intelligent code completion and analysis
- ✅ Powerful debugging and testing tools
- ✅ Git integration built-in
- ✅ Virtual environment management
- ✅ Database support (SQL, NoSQL)
- ✅ Web development support (Django, Flask)
- ✅ Remote development via SSH
- ✅ Plugin ecosystem
- ✅ Code refactoring tools
- ✅ Performance profiling

**Community vs Professional:**

| Feature | Community | Professional |
|---------|-----------|--------------|
| Python development | ✅ | ✅ |
| Django/Flask support | ❌ | ✅ |
| Database tools | ❌ | ✅ |
| Docker support | ❌ | ✅ |
| Remote development | ❌ | ✅ |
| Scientific tools | ❌ | ✅ |
| Web development | ❌ | ✅ |
| Cost | Free | $199/year |

